 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Pre-processing involves SFC indexing, which requires sorting bricks by their curve index. Exact complexity is not given in the sources.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** The BFAT is a 2D sparse matrix, storing only valid indices. Memory usage scales with the number of bricks and LODs. Exact complexity is not given in the sources.
-*   **Performance:** Enables out-of-core rendering by allowing efficient loading of bricks based on SFC locality. Performance depends on the efficiency of the Hilbert curve implementation and I/O throughput [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Cache-friendly access patterns due to SFC ordering; simple indexing via 1D arrays; supports out-of-core processing [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires pre-processing to convert regular grids to BSAMR; SFC indexing may not be optimal for all data distributions; sparse BFAT can lead to memory overhead if not implemented efficiently [S1, unofficial].
